 is still there later (pooled, fitted with each year left out) is 1.07 in Sep–Nov, 0.94 in Oct–Dec, 0.71 in Nov–Jan, 0.47 in Dec–Feb; in E it is 0.93, 0.80, 0.69, 0.54. The correction applies those weights. Out of sample it changes the multi-model error in E − C in Oct–Dec from 0.67 to 0.54, which is not statistically significant (Wilcoxon over years, p = 0.16). In 1997, the strongest east-based event in the hindcast period, the models' average for Oct–Dec had E +3.4 and C +1.2 against an observed E +4.2 and C +0.3: too central, the same direction as this year's first-month error. A regression calibration of E and C on the hindcasts does not beat the forecast as issued (0.66 in Oct–Dec).","rule":"first-month-corrected leads only if, in the hindcasts, it lowers the multi-model E − C error at the peak season with p < 0.05 (Wilcoxon over years) and raises it in no season"}}